comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T11:09:42.251Z","harness:claude-code","Two families were registered by hand in the same pass that measured this gap, which is the behaviour this item asks to make unnecessary rather than a fix for it.\n\nAdded to config/defect-recurrence-policy.json:\n- declared-set-versus-hand-maintained-list, owner pm-suhxny, escape class production_defect, historical lineage pm-b84irw, pm-te6elw, pm-1jrdri, pm-6j7r1a, pm-xpumg4, pm-7wx1f9, pm-suhxny, pm-edywqn. Eight measured instances, the largest recurrence family in the record, previously unregistered.\n- ambient-host-state-in-measured-fixture, owner pm-4o7tlx, escape class review_caught_late, historical lineage pm-t7wn04 and pm-4o7tlx.\n\nSelection proven against the built SDK with analyzeDefectChangeRisk over the parsed policy. A change touching src/mcp/legacy-adapter.ts selects declared-set-versus-hand-maintained-list, review-caught-contract-drift and security-scanner-finding. A change touching scripts/release/token-budget-gate.mjs selects ambient-host-state-in-measured-fixture and cross-platform-nightly-regression. A change touching sdk/public-surface.json selects declared-set-versus-hand-maintained-list. The negative control, a change touching only README.md, selects nothing, so the triggers discriminate rather than matching everything.\n\nPolicy validation and the scale benchmark both accept the additions: defect-evidence-gate reports PASS with 8 families and 0 findings, and defect-recurrence-index --check passes at 1,000,000 items with full 18.7s and incremental 25ms.\n\nCoverage after the additions is 16 of the 75 items in a recurrence lineage. Registering the remaining 59 by hand is not the fix and is not proposed here; deriving family coverage from the recorded lineages is."
